he hyperbola $2(y+3)^{2}-3{x}^{2}=21.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(y+3)^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 2(0+3)^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 2(3)^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 2(9)-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 18-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ -3{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, there are no $x$-intercepts." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-170553/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de185a6-24a0-55aa-905d-8893a555e331"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278368/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "093cea9e-667a-5183-b3d4-b1211936424d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278368/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff9e39c-08f8-594c-9e90-63e47778d606" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278368/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-278368/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278368/field-2/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "86021b2d-7ad1-523e-95ac-7e2e95bc78b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278368/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "af576c18-e9f3-514c-809c-d07d55b396f8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278368/field-2/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-278368/field-2/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278368" :question/id #uuid "a26f7a92-e625-525c-9ca3-0d3ed4556a84" :question/math-academy-id "q-278368" :question/problem "The $y$-intercept of the hyperbola $(x-1)^{2}-\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{3}=1$ is$\\,(${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}-\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ (0-1)^{2}-\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{3} & =0 \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y+3 & =0 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $(0,-3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278368/field-1" "q-278368/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c249cf3a-7864-5132-80fa-c18a3ea915c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278368"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10484/selection/8ab9b47516f97a0d94c1b782e3a65ae25eb4010d1bc943bf15aa85cee17eda13" :answer/id #uuid "5223c88d-2bed-518e-ab79-739ab19ef2be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\pm 5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10484/selection/cfe3a2f3227cfd9e9247397c00c9f331417642d2f9cc796a2ef2b5b74f2e0967" :answer/id #uuid "130b9090-0104-5310-a192-f4f7d09924a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\pm 4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10484/selection/aeea9004e13b73aca0bdb8410e5f0d7650e1948bb6a1e853569a6fae935de206" :answer/id #uuid "abfe4fc4-b0b1-5c16-a8f6-95d6252f776e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\pm 15)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10484/selection/ac3af717d5979e3a75b9044f25a5f3b02e4715376cbbb753b146faded1ea47b8" :answer/id #uuid "5c0f8a10-32d0-5273-b4d2-ac6c5448dd87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/va