alue "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277802/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "38224f51-3a4a-56bb-ac3b-bf80feaa664a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277802/field-4/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-277802/field-4/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277802" :question/id #uuid "e9dfffee-93ab-5b9a-91d2-b8ba63f7d71c" :question/math-academy-id "q-277802" :question/problem "From **top to bottom,** the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}=36$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-4(0)^{2} & =36 \\\\ 9{y}^{2} & =36 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,2)$ and $(0,-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-277802/field-1" "q-277802/field-2" "q-277802/field-3" "q-277802/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c249cf3a-7864-5132-80fa-c18a3ea915c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277802"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84045/selection/f30fb0f59fafb6752d784950cc322d7f2032f94280c61093320bd35b48f74686" :answer/id #uuid "0be492ed-c02e-56fe-a8ba-bae7359d68a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84045/selection/dae5335f979b458799ffc035d2adfc1f0d0e4959597eec73a82bdb6dc329f121" :answer/id #uuid "eff5e56f-23c2-5b12-8ad4-c0ece8311597" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no $y$-intercepts" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84045/selection/ac3af