\\\ -{x}^{2} & =16-25 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & =-9 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $y=2.5$  at the points $(-3,2.5)$ and $(3,2.5).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-278384/field-1" "q-278384/field-2" "q-278384/field-3" "q-278384/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "395f435d-473f-5dae-b215-2986556d5793"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278384"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278386/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e01b02c7-f65f-52b5-bdf5-edc9d534f8e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278386/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3577dc9d-f305-5bf7-b57b-d27e8534347c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278386/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-278386/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278386/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1e493414-cbfd-5554-8951-b56dd6eeef99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278386/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "764cc31d-bd41-58fe-ae98-aefa8fdf2f24" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278386/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-278386/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278386" :question/id #uuid "7a83b146-c3f6-599a-bc41-f567758cd670" :question/math-academy-id "q-278386" :question/problem "The hyperbola $6{x}^{2}-8{y}^{2}=24$ intersects the line $x=2$ at\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=2,$ we substitute $x=2$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-8{y}^{2} & =24 \\\\ 6(2)^{2}-8{y}^{2} & =24 \\\\ 24-8{y}^{2} & =24 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=2$  at $(2,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-278386/field-1" "q-278386/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "395f435d-473f-5dae-b215-2986556d5793"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278386"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278374/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "d4e1154e-7f7f-580f-b24f-cb6a0bfe9904" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278374/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "41b73486-692a-552b-98c1-6b43459cc248" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278374/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-278374/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278374/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "a967f871-6774-5123-9c0e-fa19a38c3ac7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278374/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0e04429-740a-571c-9cee-8c644701f204" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278374/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-278374/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278374" :question/id #uuid "76e113f8-fc6f-514a-9924-ec8aaae4d36b" :question/math-academy-id "q-278374" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}=1$ intersects the line $y=x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{12{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-2$ and $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-278374/field-1" "q-278374/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278374"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278378/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "9eb5a90a-24be-5f02-b5dd-561158a561cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278378/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "54fb7f73-369b-52a9-883a-9b9fd3dadcab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278378/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f30fc65-eca1-5c87-9e82-50b3df47c11e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278378/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-278378/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-278378/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278378/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0d88a308-f985-56bf-974e-50627ad00296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278378/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "bee1488a-d9ee-59cf-a553-c06ba63a2f0b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278378/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-278378/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278378" :question/id #uuid "2b2cfbfb-c2b5-564f-a50c-f6a3316ef02c" :question/math-academy-id "q-278378" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $8{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}=27$ intersects the line $y=x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2} & =27 \\\\ 8{x}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =27 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & =27 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-3$ and $x=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-278378/field-1" "q-278378/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278378"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278383/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uui